  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 17 files that constitute the full impact surface for the RealmExport schema migration:\n\n**Core schema/model**\n- `zerver/models/realm_audit_logs.py` \u2014 current `RealmAuditLog`/`AuditLogEventType.REALM_EXPORTED` + `extra_data` JSON field being replaced\n- `zerver/models/__init__.py` \u2014 model registration point (needs the new `RealmExport` import)\n- `zerver/models/realms.py` \u2014 export-type constants (`EXPORT_PUBLIC`, etc.) shared across the export code paths\n\n**Direct references**\n- `zerver/actions/realm_export.py` \u2014 actions layer (`notify_realm_export`, `do_delete_realm_export`)\n- `zerver/views/realm_export.py` \u2014 views serving export status/CRUD to the frontend\n- `zerver/lib/export.py` \u2014 `get_realm_exports_serialized`, `export_realm_wrapper`, `do_export_realm`\n\n**Indirect/tentacle references**\n- `zerver/worker/deferred_work.py` \u2014 background worker running the actual export job\n- `zerver/management/commands/export.py` and `export_usermessage_batch.py` \u2014 CLI export tooling\n- `zerver/lib/import_realm.py` \u2014 writes `REALM_EXPORTED`-adjacent audit rows on import\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `zerver/tests/test_realm_export.py` \u2014 dedicated export endpoint tests\n- `zerver/tests/test_import_export.py` \u2014 import/export round-trip tests\n- `zerver/tests/test_events.py` \u2014 event schema tests referencing `REALM_EXPORTED`\n- `zerver/tests/test_management_commands.py` \u2014 CLI command tests\n\n**Frontend/API contract**\n- `web/src/settings_exports.ts` \u2014 TS schema (`realm_export_schema`) consuming the export status JSON\n- `zerver/openapi/zulip.yaml` \u2014 `RealmExport` API schema definition\n\n**Migration context**\n- `zerver/migrations/0594_remove_realm_user_group_edit_policy.py` \u2014 confirms 0595 is the correct next migration number and its dependency chain\n\nNote: today's tracking isn't literally a JSON file on disk \u2014 it's the `extra_data` JSONField on `RealmAuditLog` rows (event_type `REALM_EXPORTED`), which is what the new `RealmExport` table replaces.",
